  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nHigh pressure across the area will weaken as low pressure develops\nalong the West Coast and the adjacent eastern Pacific. High\ntemperatures will cool a few degrees on Friday and another 4 to 8\ndegrees on Saturday with high temperatures on Saturday still\naround 5 degrees above average. High temperatures on Saturday will\nrange from the mid 70s to the lower 80s near the coast to the mid\n80s to lower 90s for the Inland Empire with the lower deserts in \nthe upper 90s. \n\nOn Sunday into early next week, that low pressure system along the\nWest Coast and off the coast of Baja may draw moisture from what\nwas Hurricane Rachel northeastward and into the area with a chance\nof showers. For early Sunday to early Tuesday, the NBM chance for\n0.10 inch or more of rainfall is 30 to 40 percent for the coast \nto the mountains with the chance for 0.50 or more 15 to 25 percent\nand the chance for 1 inch or more 10 to 15 percent.\n\nHigh temperatures for the coast and valleys will cool from the mid\n70s to lower 80s on Sunday to the 70s on Monday with the lower \ndeserts cooling from the lower 90s on Sunday to the 80s on Monday.",
